# Movie Finder Infrastructure — Cursor Rules

This file is a legacy fallback. Cursor loads the richer MDC rules from `.cursor/rules/` automatically.

If your IDE supports MDC rules, the following files apply:
- `.cursor/rules/project.mdc` — always active (infrastructure context, Docker-only workflow)
- `.cursor/rules/architect.mdc` — activates on `**/*.tf`, `**/*.bicep`, `**/*.puml`, `**/*.dsl`
- `.cursor/rules/developer.mdc` — activates when implementing IaC changes

---

## Quick reference

**Repo:** `aharbii/movie-finder-infrastructure` · Primary context: `CLAUDE.md`

**Non-negotiables:**
- All local work runs Docker-only (`make shell`, `make check`) — never run `terraform` directly on host
- Never commit secrets or `.env` files — new secrets go to Azure Key Vault manually
- Never bake secrets into Docker images or pass them through CI logs
- Terraform changes must be idempotent
- `make check` (fmt-check + validate + tflint) must pass before any PR
- Conventional Commits: `chore(infra): summary`
- Disclose AI tool + model in every PR
